<title>INDIA: India STC tender for wheat imports closes Monday.</title>
<headline>India STC tender for wheat imports closes Monday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run State Trading Corporation (STC) said on Saturday that a tender floated for the import of 50,000 tonnes of wheat would close on Monday at 10.00 a.m. (0430 GMT).</p>
<p>&quot;The tender floated on Thursday for the import of 50,000 tonnes of wheat will close on Monday at 10 a.m.,&quot; Deepak Prasad, director of STC, told Reuters.</p>
<p>But the quantity actually bought by STC would depend on the prices quoted by the sellers, Prasad said.</p>
<p>India said on Thursday it would buy two million tonnes of wheat in 1996/97 (April-March) to augment domestic supplies and check rising prices.</p>
<p>STC said on Friday that it had bought one million tonnes of wheat from Australia for delivery starting in January.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
